.TH MKFS.OCSFS 8 "March 2026" "ocsfs 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mkfs.ocsfs \- create an OCSFS filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfs.ocsfs
[\fB\-L\fR \fIlabel\fR]
[\fB\-N\fR \fImax-nodes\fR]
[\fB\-J\fR \fIjournal-size\fR]
[\fB\-A\fR \fIag-size\fR]
[\fB\-B\fR \fIblock-size\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
.I device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkfs.ocsfs
creates an OCSFS (Open Cluster Shared FileSystem) on the specified
block device or image file. OCSFS is a cluster-aware filesystem
designed for shared Fibre Channel SAN storage in virtualized environments.
.PP
The formatted volume includes:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Primary and mirror superblocks
.IP \(bu 2
Node slot table (for cluster membership)
.IP \(bu 2
Heartbeat area (for failure detection)
.IP \(bu 2
Lock table (for distributed locking)
.IP \(bu 2
Per-AG block bitmaps and inode tables
.IP \(bu 2
Per-node journal regions
.IP \(bu 2
Root directory inode
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-L " " \fIlabel\fR
Set the volume label (up to 64 characters).
.TP
.BR \-N " " \fImax-nodes\fR
Maximum number of cluster nodes (1\-256, default 64).
Each node requires a dedicated journal region.
.TP
.BR \-J " " \fIjournal-size\fR
Per-node journal size (e.g. "32M", "64M"). Default: 32 MiB.
.TP
.BR \-A " " \fIag-size\fR
Allocation Group size (e.g. "1G", "512M"). Default: 1 GiB.
Smaller AG sizes increase concurrency but add metadata overhead.
.TP
.BR \-B " " \fIblock-size\fR
Block size in bytes (default 4096). Must be a power of 2.
.TP
.BR \-f
Force formatting even if the device appears to contain data.
.TP
.BR \-v
Verbose output \- print detailed layout information.
.SH EXAMPLES
Format a 2 TiB SAN LUN for a 16-node Proxmox cluster:
.PP
.RS 4
mkfs.ocsfs \-L pve\-shared \-N 16 \-f \-v /dev/mapper/mpath\-3600508b...
.RE
.PP
Format a test image:
.PP
.RS 4
dd if=/dev/zero of=/tmp/test.img bs=1M count=2048
.br
mkfs.ocsfs \-L test \-N 2 \-f /tmp/test.img
.RE
